entries_with_gt.problem:
Given the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
&\frac{2 + 3i}{1 - i} = z_1 \\
&\frac{4 + 5i}{2 - i} = z_2
\end{align*}
Find the value of $|z_1|^{2} - \text{Re}(z_1) + \text{Im}(z_1) + |z_2|^{2} - \text{Re}(z_2) + \text{Im}(z_2)$.

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) satisfying the system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
3x \equiv 1 \pmod{14} \\
5x \equiv 3 \pmod{7} \\
4x \equiv 2 \pmod{11}
\end{cases}
\]
